From 572df0f1e5cb586e67ad994918d2e36c4d67d852 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Raza <raza@bukc.edu.pk>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 19:28:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(profile): notification inbox, Profile screen for every
 role (AUTH-17/20)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Your notification table and enum already existed and were actively used
by Borrow/Venue — nothing ever read them back, and Auth never wrote to
them despite AUTH-20 requiring an in-app notification alongside the
account-verification email. This builds the missing read side plus the
AUTH-20 write, and gives every role the Profile screen AUTH-17 implies
('change your own password from your profile').

DATABASE (migration 016): two new notification_type values,
ACCOUNT_DEACTIVATED / ACCOUNT_REACTIVATED, same pattern as migration 007.

SERVER:
- New notifications feature: list/unread-count/mark-read/mark-all-read,
  every route strictly scoped to the caller's own inbox (no admin
  'view anyone's notifications' surface — this is personal).
- verifyAccount() now writes ACCOUNT_VERIFIED alongside its existing
  email (the actual AUTH-20 requirement); deactivateAccount()/
  reactivateAccount() do the same for consistency.
- GET /api/auth/me upgraded from {userId, role} into a full profile
  fetch (getMyProfile), reusing the same student/external join already
  built for the Active Accounts tab.
- GET /api/borrow/reputation/:userId now also allows self-access (a
  student can see their own reputation, previously staff-only) — needed
  for the Profile screen's stats section.

CLIENT:
- Removed the dev-mode 'invite link' box from Invite a Coordinator —
  real email delivery is the actual flow now.
- New ProfileScreen, reachable via 'My Profile' from every role's home
  screen: notification inbox (click to mark read, mark-all-read),
  read-only personal details, a change-password form (AUTH-17, the
  endpoint existed with zero UI before this), and a role-specific
  activity section — Student gets reputation stats + recent borrow
  requests with a link to My Borrows, External gets recent venue
  bookings with a link to Book a Venue. Coordinator/Super Admin get the
  base profile (details + notifications + password) without an activity
  section — see the chat writeup for the reasoning on why.

Tests: 7 new (notifications.test.ts) covering the AUTH-20 write, unread
count math, mark-read/mark-all-read, cross-user isolation (can't mark
someone else's notification, 404 not 403 — no existence leak), and
ordering. Plus a new borrow.test.ts case confirming self-access to
reputation works and cross-student access is still blocked (403).

Verified against a real local Postgres: migrations 001-016 apply
cleanly, seed runs, tsc --noEmit clean on both sides, full suite
136/137 (the one failure is the pre-existing Asia/Karachi same-day
timing flake in T-610, confirmed unrelated — same flake identified
earlier in this project, reproducible only near local midnight in
Karachi, byte-identical date logic to origin/main).
